        ":question/id": "287c4c83-1be4-5535-a78c-1deaf55cde76",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-125370",
        ":question/problem": "Let $F(x,y,z)={y}^{2}\\,i-{x}^{2}\\,j+5\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+5\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
