        ":question/id": "ab23b1e6-350e-57c6-bc34-78c226b2bb0d",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-125416",
        ":question/problem": "Let $F(x,y)=(x-3y)\\,i+2\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2}+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
