        ":question/problem": "If ${\\int }_{C}(y-z)\\,\\text{d}x+6{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P=y-z,Q=6{z}^{2},R=-4y.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}((y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}(y-z)\\,\\text{d}x+6{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F=(y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k.$"
